: "hot", "size": "m", "bold": true, "visible": "leg==0"}, {"type": "text", "id": "h2_0", "at": [6.45, 8.75], "text": "Heat \\(Q_1\\) flows IN  ·  \\(T\\) stays \\(T_1\\)", "role": "wall", "size": "s", "bold": false, "visible": "leg==0"}, {"type": "text", "id": "h1_1", "at": [6.45, 9.4], "text": "\\(b\\to c\\)  Adiabatic expansion", "role": "adB", "size": "m", "bold": true, "visible": "leg==1"}, {"type": "text", "id": "h2_1", "at": [6.45, 8.75], "text": "No heat flow  ·  gas cools \\(T_1\\to T_2\\)", "role": "wall", "size": "s", "bold": false, "visible": "leg==1"}, {"type": "text", "id": "h1_2", "at": [6.45, 9.4], "text": "\\(c\\to d\\)  Isothermal compression", "role": "cold", "size": "m", "bold": true, "visible": "leg==2"}, {"type": "text", "id": "h2_2", "at": [6.45, 8.75], "text": "Heat \\(Q_2\\) flows OUT  ·  \\(T\\) stays \\(T_2\\)", "role": "wall", "size": "s", "bold": false, "visible": "leg==2"}, {"type": "text", "id": "h1_3", "at": [6.45, 9.4], "text": "\\(d\\to a\\)  Adiabatic compression", "role": "adD", "size": "m", "bold": true, "visible": "leg==3"}, {"type": "text", "id": "h2_3", "at": [6.45, 8.75], "text": "No heat flow  ·  gas warms \\(T_2\\to T_1\\)", "role": "wall", "size": "s", "bold": false, "visible": "leg==3"}, {"type": "segment", "id": "bbase", "from": [9.3, 10.05], "to": [12.85, 10.05], "role": "wall", "strokeWidth": 2}, {"type": "rect", "id": "bar0", "x": 9.45, "y": 10.05, "w": 0.8, "h": "max(0.04, abs(bA)/bmax*2.6)", "role": "hot", "fill": true, "fillOpacity": 0.55, "strokeWidth": 2}, {"type": "text", "id": "bn0", "at": [9.85, 13.649999999999999], "text": "\\(Q_1\\)", "role": "hot", "size": "s", "bold": true}, {"type": "text", "id": "bv0", "at": [9.85, "10.05+max(0.04, abs(bA)/bmax*2.6)+0.32"], "text": "{{bA|int}}", "role": "hot", "size": "s", "bold": true}, {"type": "rect", "id": "bar1", "x": 10.649999999999999, "y": 10.05, "w": 0.8, "h": "max(0.04, abs(bW)/bmax*2.6)", "role": "work", "fill": true, "fillOpacity": 0.55, "strokeWidth": 2}, {"type": "text", "id": "bn1", "at": [11.049999999999999, 13.649999999999999], "text": "\\(W\\)", "role": "work", "size": "s", "bold": true}, {"type": "text", "id": "bv1", "at": [11.049999999999999, "10.05+max(0.04, abs(bW)/bmax*2.6)+0.32"], "text": "{{bW|int}}", "role": "work", "size": "s", "bold": true}, {"type": "rect", "id": "bar2", "x": 11.85, "y": 10.05, "w": 0.8, "h": "max(0.04, abs(bB)/bmax*2.6)", "role": "cold", "fill": true, "fillOpacity": 0.55, "strokeWidth": 2}, {"type": "text", "id": "bn2", "at": [12.25, 13.649999999999999], "text": "\\(Q_2\\)", "role": "cold", "size": "s", "bold": true}, {"type": "text", "id": "bv2", "at": [12.25, "10.05+max(0.04, abs(bB)/bmax*2.6)+0.32"], "text": "{{bB|int}}", "role": "cold", "size": "s", "bold": true}], "steps": [{"id": "s0", "title": "Where are we?", "text": "The cylinder sits on the **hot** reservoir at \\(T_1 = {{T1|0}}\\) K. The gas starts at point \\(a\\) with pressure \\(P_1\\) and volume \\(V_1\\). Its temperature is \\(T_1\\).", "actions": [{"set": {"ph": 0}, "at": 0}], "dwell": 5200}, {"id": "s1", "title": "Let it expand", "text": "The gas pushes the piston out. Expanding gas wants to cool, but the hot reservoir keeps pouring heat in, so \\(T\\) stays at \\(T_1\\). Because \\(PV = nRT_1\\) is constant, \\(P\\) falls as \\(1/V\\): the curve is a hyperbola.", "actions": [{"tween": {"ph": 1}, "at": 0, "dur": 4200}], "dwell": 6000}, {"id": "s2", "title": "Energy bookkeeping", "text": "For an ideal gas \\(U\\) depends only on \\(T\\). \\(T\\) is constant, so \\(\\Delta U = 0\\) and by the first law \\(Q = W\\). So far: \\(Q = {{Ql|int}}\\) J in, \\(W = {{Wl|int}}\\) J out, \\(\\Delta U = {{dUl|int}}\\) J.", "actions": [{"set": {"ph": 1}, "at": 0}], "dwell": 5200}, {"id": "s3", "title": "Area = work", "text": "The shaded area under the curve is the work done **by** the gas: \\(W_{ab} = nRT_1\\ln\\dfrac{V_2}{V_1}\\). With 1 mol this is \\({{Q1|0}}\\) J, and that is exactly the heat \\(Q_1\\) taken from the hot reservoir.", "actions": [{"set": {"ph": 1}, "at": 0}], "dwell": 5200}, {"id": "s4", "title": "Remember", "text": "Heat in, volume up, temperature constant at \\(T_1\\). This is the **only** stroke where the engine takes in heat.", "actions": [{"set": {"ph": 1}, "at": 0}], "dwell": 5200}], "readouts": [{"label": "Heat in so far", "value": "{{Ql|int}} J", "role": "hot"}, {"label": "Work by gas so far", "value": "{{Wl|int}} J", "role": "work"}, {"label": "Internal energy change", "value": "{{dUl|int}} J", "role": "u"}, {"label": "Temperature now", "value": "{{T|0}} K", "role": "me"}], "formulas": [{"title": "Isothermal expansion", "tex": "Q_1 = W_{ab} = nRT_1\\ln\\dfrac{V_2}{V_1},\\quad \\Delta U = 0", "text": "Heat absorbed equals work done by the gas."}, {"title": "Work as an area", "tex": "W = \\int P\\,dV = \\text{area under the curve}", "text": "Positive when the gas expands, negative when it is compressed."}], "challenges": [{"id": "c1", "type": "choice", "title": "Now you try", "prompt": "During a→b the temperature of the gas…", "options": [{"id": "a", "label": "rises"}, {"id": "b", "label": "stays at \\(T_1\\)"}, {"id": "c", "label": "falls to \\(T_2\\)"}], "answer": "b", "hint": "The gas is in contact with a reservoir.", "explain": "The hot reservoir replaces every joule the gas spends on work, so \\(T = T_1\\) throughout."}, {"id": "c2", "type": "number", "title": "Now you try", "prompt": "A gas (1 mol, \\(R = 8.314\\) J/mol K) expands isothermally at \\(500\\) K to twice its volume. How much heat \\(Q_1\\) (in J) does it absorb?", "answer": "8.314*T1*ln(Vr)", "hint": "Use \\(Q_1 = nRT_1\\ln(V_2/V_1)\\).", "explain": "\\(Q_1 = 8.314 \\times 500 \\times \\ln 2 \\approx 2881\\) J.", "unit": "J", "set": {"T1": 500, "Vr": 2.0}}], "takeaways": ["Heat in, volume up, temperature constant at \\(T_1\\). This is the **only** stroke where the engine takes in heat."]}